 {:seon.task/name "a-source-fact-the-store-refuses-loses-nothing"
  :seon.task/plan "Found 2026-11-05 on jolt/simpler-schema, in seon.source-test/main-s-program-follows-the-checkout-while-root-runs-and-across-a-restart: when the source import failed (seon.source/unanalyzable), the store refused root's source fact (konserve.jolt.fasl: no stable encoding for clojure.lang.PersistentTreeMap), and seon.root/import-source! appended that to :error, so the fact's own values were lost. Cause to find: which value of the failed import's fact is a sorted map. Correct: the fact is plain data (seon.contract/plainly at its write, or the value's owner), and the failure stays readable. Reproduce by making a source form the analyzer rejects. Since: the docstring of `seon.root/import-source!` states that a fact the store refuses is a :platform cause with the writer's reason, and that the fact in force is then this boot's without its inputs, saying why (:error); not reproduced here, so whether the sorted-map value is still written is not known."
